    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, you don't need the specific transcript to speak to the logic of it. if a witness comes forward with specific, eye-witness data about ballot handling and the lawyers just shut it down by saying \"it's hearsay\" without actually addressing the specifics, isn't that just a way to avoid the truth? it feels like one side is using legal technicalities to bury real concerns. shouldn't an objective analysis recognize that dismissing evidence without debunking it is different from actually proving it wrong?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
